Literature sweep completed 2026-05-04.

Effector identification (resolved):
- PBY2 is a MAX-fold avirulence effector from Pyricularia oryzae (barley blast
  pathotype, isolate Br48). Signal peptide residues 1-20; mature chain 21-85
  (65 residues). GenBank accession range: LC905591-LC905597 (Asuke et al. 2025).
- Recognised by Rmo2 (barley TKP, gene ABC1037) via its N-terminal integrated
  HMA domain (1-77 of the Rmo2 protein). KD = 53.5 nM by ITC (Yu et al. 2025).
- Binding-critical effector residue: E42 (precursor numbering); E42R abolishes
  binding to Rmo2-HMA and resistance in barley in planta.

Source PDB and numbering convention:
- Chain A: AF3 monomer prediction of native Pikp-1 HMA (UniProt E9KPB5,
  residues 186-263), renumbered 1-78 (pipeline = literature - 185). Shared
  with all pikp1_* campaigns.
- Chain B: PBY2 coordinates from PDB 9TFO chain B (Rmo2-HMA/PBY2, 2.2 A,
  Yu et al. 2025; currently HPUB on-hold). Numbering likely precursor (1-85);
  verify in ChimeraX that residue 42 = Glu (E42).
- Complex assembly: cross-system alignment. Superpose AF3 Pikp-1 HMA (chain A)
  onto 9TFO chain A (Rmo2-HMA, 1-77), then adopt PBY2 chain B coordinates from
  9TFO. 6G10 and 6Q76 are NOT used — PBY2 binds a third, distinct face of the
  HMA fold.
- Fallback: if 9TFO is inaccessible, run AF3-multimer of Pikp-1 HMA + PBY2
  (rung 7). PBY2 sequence available from GenBank LC905591-LC905597.

Binding face determination (CAMPAIGN-SPECIFIC; distinct from all sibling campaigns):
- PBY2 binds the BETA-3 FACE of Rmo2-HMA (β3 strand antiparallel with β2 of
  PBY2; predominantly main-chain), with limited side-chain contacts from Rmo2-HMA
  α1 (D15, K18) to PBY2 β2 (E42, S48).
- This is spatially distinct from the canonical AVR-Pik face (β4/β3 pairing used
  in 6G10/5A6W etc.) and from the AVR-Pia face (β2/αA pairing used in 6Q76/5ZNG).
- On Pikp-1 HMA in pipeline numbering, the equivalent of β3 of Rmo2-HMA is
  approximately pipeline positions 43-49 (β3 strand of Pikp-1 HMA).
- Primary redesign target: pipeline ~42-51 (β3 + flanking loops).
- This region was ANCHORED in pikp1_avrpikf and pikp1_avrpia — the PBY2 campaign
  requires a distinct contig.

Primary contig:
  A1-41/10-18/A52-78 B

Primary papers cited:
- Yu et al. 2025 bioRxiv (9TFO/9TFP/9TFQ/9TFS/9TFT; Rmo2-HMA/PBY2 structure;
  binding interface; E42R mutagenesis; KD; TKP engineering)
- Asuke et al. 2025 bioRxiv (Rmo2 cloning; PBY2 cloning; PBY2 = MAX effector;
  GenBank sequence; Rmo2/PBY2 biology; PBY2 distribution in pathotypes)
- Maqbool 2015 eLife (Pikp-1 HMA scaffold; AVR-Pik canonical face)
- De la Concepcion 2018 Nat Plants (Interface 1/2/3 definition; Pikp-HMA fold)
- Guo 2018 PNAS (distinct binding surfaces; AVR1-CO39/RGA5 β2/β2 face)
- Varden 2019 JBC (AVR-Pia/Pikp-HMA α1/β2 face; showing β3 face is distinct)
- Reveguk 2025 Nat Genet (TKP integrated domains review)
- Nga et al. 2012 Phytopathology (RMO2 locus identification)

Source provenance:
- Read from experiments/inputs/context/:
  - yu_2025_bioarxiv.pdf (Yu et al. 2025 bioRxiv — structural data, binding face,
    PDB codes, E42R mutagenesis, KD)
  - asuke_2025_bioarxiv.pdf (Asuke et al. 2025 bioRxiv — Rmo2 cloning, PBY2
    cloning, MAX fold confirmation, GenBank accessions, pathotype distribution)
  - guo_2018_pnas.pdf (for comparison of binding faces)
  - delaconcepcion_2019_natplants.pdf (Pikp-1 HMA scaffold; reused)
- Fetched online (RCSB PDB only): 9TFO, 9TFP metadata (HPUB status confirmed).
- Receptor-scaffold papers (Maqbool 2015, Varden 2019, etc.): reused from
  sibling pikp1_avrpikf and pikp1_avrpia sweeps.

No campaign-blockers: PBY2 coordinates (9TFO chain B), structural binding-face
data, mutagenesis data, and PBY2 sequence (GenBank) are all available.
